-- id: exp6827-chronological-causal-edge-memory-stream
-  title: Chronological causal-edge verified-memory stream
-  track: continuous-self-learning
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 180
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.08.596
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6827_chronological_causal_edge_memory_stream.json
-  gated_on:
-    - upstream: exp6826-selective-arbiter-sealed-adoption
-      artifact_field: selective_arbiter_audit_complete
-      op: '=='
-      value: true
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6812 supplies authentic outputs from all three mandated GGUF families. Exp6826 supplies a
-    sealed component-level arbiter decision. CaSKG (arXiv:2608.25500) calibrates procedural edges
-    with remove, substitute, and reorder counterfactuals. Build the frozen chronological stream for
-    external memory learning. This task does not learn and invokes no LLM.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/research-program.md, Continuous Self-Learning
-    - {project_root}/_bmad/prd.md, FR11
-    - {project_root}/research-references.md, V596 Planner Refresh
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6798_csl_causal_safety_byte_audit.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6812_sota_operational_handoff_corpus_v2.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6826_selective_arbiter_sealed_adoption.json
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/memory/transactional_constraint_memory.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/continuous-learning/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Convert authentic proposals and independently audited receipts into a bounded chronological
-    verified-memory stream. Define typed add, revise, soft-delete, retrieve, filter, and restore
-    operations. Add remove, substitute, and reorder counterfactuals for candidate causal edges.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require selective_arbiter_audit_complete=true, all three source families,
-       raw hashes, terminal component decisions, chronological keys, legal alternatives, and no
-       future fields in decision snapshots. On failure write complete_blocked_chronological_
-       causal_edge_memory_stream with gate_check_summary and stop.
-    1. Write tests first for typed operations, canonical ordering, soft-delete visibility, restore
-       authority, read-only snapshots, sealed outcomes, split isolation, counterfactual edges, and
-       byte-stable serialization.
-    2. Define fixed-capacity state and a public operation grammar. Each operation has an exact
-       precondition, deterministic effect, inverse or rollback target, and canonical bytes.
-    3. Order events without family pooling. Seal outcome, utility, support, retention, hard-case,
-       later-read, and audit fields until after each decision. Freeze five chronological orders,
-       held-future partitions, and three leave-one-family-out rotations.
-    4. Generate candidate edges and remove, substitute, and reorder counterfactuals. The stream may
-       include learner-proposed tests, but final acceptance fields remain in a hidden harness view.
-    5. Require nonzero legal alternatives, safe no-op events, conflicts, admissible and rejected
-       writes, later retrieval opportunities, and stale-pressure recovery cases.
-    6. Emit one row per event-order-family-counterfactual unit. Set verified_memory_stream_ready
-       from complete chronology, headroom, sealed fields, and canonical bytes, independent of the
-       arbiter adoption outcome.
-    7. Run focused tests, ruff, OpenSpec coverage, continuous-learning E2E checks, adversarial
-       verification, artifact convention audit, verdict-row consistency lint, and root-clutter
-       checks.
-    8. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS AND PRINCIPLES: field_principles (one principle per field);
-       inference_substrate (CPU transformation of frozen authentic outputs, no LLM); duration_s
-       (measured wall time); random_seed (frozen order, split, and counterfactual seeds);
-       reproducibility_checksum (bind sources, schema, rows, commands, and output);
-       source_artifact_hashes (proposal and sealed-audit identity); operation_schema (bounded typed
-       operations); local_receipt_schema (exact precondition and effect); capacity_contract (equal
-       finite memory); split_manifest (development, held-future, hard-case, and rotations);
-       sealed_field_manifest (hidden outcome and acceptance fields); order_hashes (chronology);
-       feature_allowlist (past state only); feature_denylist (future, family oracle, and outcome
-       fields); causal_edge_schema (write-read-action-outcome identity); counterfactual_manifest
-       (remove, substitute, and reorder units); rows (every event-order-family-counterfactual unit);
-       headroom_metrics (alternatives and later reads); admissible_operation_count (nonzero);
-       rejected_operation_count (nonzero); later_read_opportunity_count (nonzero);
-       verified_memory_stream_ready (exact field consumed by Exp6828); gate_check_summary (failed
-       check, expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict); verifier_is_oracle
-       (false, this is a frozen stream); verdict_class (closed enum: positive | circular_positive |
-       null | blocked | disqualified | partial); honest_verdict (terminal and row-supported).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6827_chronological_causal_edge_memory_stream.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
